solid-state drives. The company's answer is high bandwidth flash, NAND stacked with the

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:41.200
same through-silicon via as used for HBM, aimed at about half the bandwidth of same generation

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:47.140
HBM, and more than 10 times the capacity. A July draft is supposed to become a finished

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:52.740
specification next January, with Sandisk and Cloud providers including Google in the standards

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:59.720
work. Money today reported that 3D stacked DRAM, sitting on the GPU or NPU, could

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:03.380
deliver about 10 times HBM bandwidth at about half the power.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.840
AGA reported dozens of times more input output pathways and a large power cut.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.220
Those are different claims and both are in today's coverage.

